# Bytecode Virtual Machine (in C)

A stack-based bytecode virtual machine and interpreter, built in C while working through
Robert Nystrom's [*Crafting Interpreters*](https://craftinginterpreters.com/).

## Status
🚧 In progress — currently through Chapter 14 (Chunks of Bytecode)

## What's implemented so far
- `Chunk` struct to store compiled bytecode instructions and constants
- A dynamic, growable array implementation from scratch (avoids fixed-size buffer limits)
- Basic disassembler to decode and print bytecode instructions for debugging

## What's next
- Value/constant handling
- The virtual machine execution loop
- Expression parsing and compilation

## Why I'm building this
I wanted to understand how languages actually work under the hood — how source code
becomes something a computer can execute. This project is my way of learning that from
the ground up in C, rather than just using existing interpreters/compilers as black boxes.

## Build & Run
```bash
gcc -o clox *.c
./clox
```

## Reference
Built by following *Crafting Interpreters* by Robert Nystrom — a fantastic resource if
you want to understand interpreter/compiler design from first principles.